    "body": "As tensions rise across the Indo-Pacific, resilient networks, cyber defense and multinational information sharing are becoming increasingly critical to military readiness and deterrence.\nAt AFCEA’s TechNet Indo-Pacific 2026, senior military leaders and defense experts outlined the challenges facing US and allied forces, from persistent electronic warfare threats on the Korean Peninsula to the evolving Taiwan conflict timeline and the need for stronger regional data-sharing capabilities.\nThis eBook brings together Breaking Defense’s coverage of the conference, highlighting the technologies, strategies and partnerships shaping the future of the Indo-Pacific battlespace.\nSign up below to receive your free copy.\nBy filling out the form you agree to receive messages from Breaking Defense and its partners.",
